</td></tr><tr><th colspan="6">Music</th><td colspan="14" data-attr-param="music"><a href="/w/Autumn_Voyage" title="Autumn Voyage">Autumn Voyage</a>, <a href="/w/Dream_(music_track)" title="Dream (music track)">Dream</a>, <a href="/w/Harmony" title="Harmony">Harmony</a></td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" class="infobox-padding"></td></tr><tr><th colspan="20" class="infobox-subheader">Map</th></tr><tr><td colspan="20" class="infobox-image infobox-full-width-content" data-attr-param="map"><a class="mw-kartographer-map mw-kartographer-container center" style="width: 300px; height: 300px;background-image: url(https://maps.runescape.wiki/rs/versions/2026-10-12-a/map_icon_squares/28/1/0_24_25.png), url(https://maps.runescape.wiki/rs/versions/2026-10-12-a/map_icon_squares/28/1/0_25_25.png), url(https://maps.runescape.wiki/rs/versions/2026-10-12-a/map_icon_squares/28/1/0_24_24.png), url(https://maps.runescape.wiki/rs/versions/2026-10-12-a/map_icon_squares/28/1/0_25_24.png); background-position: -106px -76px, 150px -76px, -106px 180px, 150px 180px; background-repeat: no-repeat;" data-mw-kartographer="" data-width="300" data-height="300" data-zoom="1" data-lat="3215" data-lon="3200" data-mapid="28" data-plane="0"></a></td></tr></tbody><caption class="advanced-data infobox-bottom-links"><a href="/w/Template:Infobox_Location" title="Template:Infobox Location">[view]</a> &#8226; <a href="/w/Template_talk:Infobox_Location" title="Template talk:Infobox Location">[talk]</a></caption></table>
<figure class="mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File"><a href="/w/File:Lumbridge_standard.png" class="mw-file-description"><img src="/images/thumb/Lumbridge_standard.png/100px-Lumbridge_standard.png?bf04b" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="100" height="179" class="mw-file-element" srcset="/images/thumb/Lumbridge_standard.png/200px-Lumbridge_standard.png?bf04b 2x" data-file-width="651" data-file-height="1166" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>
<p><b>Lumbridge</b> is a town in the kingdom of <a href="/w/Misthalin" title="Misthalin">Misthalin</a>, ruled by <a href="/w/Duke_Horacio" title="Duke Horacio">Duke Horacio</a> from the <a href="/w/Lumbridge_Castle" title="Lumbridge Castle">Lumbridge Castle</a>. It is located in the southern part of the kingdom on the banks of the <a href="/w/River_Lum" title="River Lum">River Lum</a>, from which it derives its name. Largely a farming town, it is protected by the <a href="/w/Lumbridge_Guard" title="Lumbridge Guard">Lumbridge Guard</a> against threats such as <a href="/w/Goblins" title="Goblins">goblins</a>, who occupy the east bank of the river.
</p><p>It is the first town that new players enter after completing the tutorial, and is home to various low level activities and <a href="/w/Quests" title="Quests">quests</a>. On the west side of the river the town has a <a href="/w/General_store" class="mw-redirect" title="General store">general store</a>, a <a href="/w/Hank%27s_Fishing_Shop" class="mw-redirect" title="Hank&#39;s Fishing Shop">fishing shop</a>, a market with a <a href="/w/Bank" title="Bank">bank</a> and <a href="/w/Thieving" title="Thieving">Thieving</a> stalls as well as a smithy with a <a href="/w/Forge" title="Forge">forge</a> and an <a href="/w/Anvil" title="Anvil">anvil</a> and an entrance to the <a href="/w/Thieves%27_Guild" title="Thieves&#39; Guild">Thieves' Guild</a>. The east side primarily features a large cow pen. The river itself has several <a href="/w/Fishing" title="Fishing">Fishing</a> spots. The southern part of the town houses a church with a graveyard and an entrance to the <a href="/w/Lumbridge_Catacombs" title="Lumbridge Catacombs">Lumbridge Catacombs</a> and a passage to the <a href="/w/Lumbridge_Swamp" title="Lumbridge Swamp">Lumbridge Swamp</a>. The city of <a href="/w/Dorgesh-Kaan" title="Dorgesh-Kaan">Dorgesh-Kaan</a> can be accessed from the castle's basement. West of the castle lies the <a href="/w/Lumbridge_forest" title="Lumbridge forest">Lumbridge forest</a>.
</p><p>Lumbridge is one of the default <a href="/w/Respawn_point" class="mw-redirect" title="Respawn point">respawn points</a> for players who <a href="/w/Death_(mechanic)" title="Death (mechanic)">die</a>, available to choose when leaving <a href="/w/Death%27s_office" title="Death&#39;s office">Death's office</a>.
</p>
